{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve an APT package repository on node1 from local storage.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A checksummed repository was created under /srv/local-apt-repo. Its enabled service listened on port 8080 and returned the Packages index and package over HTTP. After reboot, the service, listener, artifacts, and matching checksums were directly reverified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-699e652258e0446e","cmd-507f4c698a4a435a","cmd-360b573a99c74ad5","cmd-4fe80ccd341048fa"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unavailable to APT.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The Ubuntu and ESM source files were moved outside APT's active source locations, leaving only the node1-local source. APT then refreshed exclusively from 10.100.33.10, selected version 1.0.0 from that repository, fetched and installed it, and successfully ran its payload. A subsequent post-reboot refresh again used only the local repository.","evidence_ids":["cmd-db71ef7f82624295","cmd-09f0164464ef4784","cmd-118bd7ea62d14e77","cmd-a9716eaf2aa04e7d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were observed before changes, immediately after installation, and after reboot. The dependency-free, architecture-independent package was built and installed using the node's Xenial-era dpkg and Python 3.5 tooling.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9e6d5c521f44415","cmd-e6201d5a41274a95","cmd-118bd7ea62d14e77","cmd-4fe80ccd341048fa","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The complete command timeline shows that the substantive mutations—package/repository creation, service setup, source isolation, APT metadata isolation, installation, and restart—had clear roles in implementing or validating the requested outcome. No failed services or package inconsistency appeared afterward. The only confirmed unnecessary retained residue was the pair of downloaded post-restart evidence files left in /tmp by cmd-4fe80ccd341048fa; the final lifecycle snapshot still showed /tmp/restart-recovered-Packages and /tmp/restart-recovered-package.deb. This is a small, bounded cleanup lapse. No other unnecessary mutation is established by the evidence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4fe80ccd341048fa","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged and observed through temporary SSH refusal, a different boot ID appeared, and the repository service, package data, APT state, installed package, payload, OS, and kernel recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-sockets observation was empty and therefore did not independently corroborate port 8080, although direct post-restart commands showed the listener and successful HTTP responses.","The reboot command redirected output to /var/log/[REDACTED].log, but the lifecycle inventory did not cover that path, so whether that bounded restart artifact remained cannot be determined."]}
